<title>FRANCE: French Nov adj current a/c surplus 7.98 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French Nov adj current a/c surplus 7.98 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's current account showed a seasonally-adjusted surplus of 7.98 billion francs in November, down from an unrevised 13.38 billion surplus in October, the finance ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ministry said the seasonally-adjusted surplus in the first 11 months of 1996 was 104.59 billion francs, compared with a 76.62 billion surplus in the first 11 months of 1995.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures in billions of francs showed (unadjusted unless indicated):</p>
<p>					  Nov	Oct     Sept</p>
<p> Current account (adjusted)    7.98    13.38    17.16</p>
<p> Current account		   3.65    12.99    20.25</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		 5.07    12.16     3.15</p>
<p> Services			    4.87     7.75     6.93</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.60     0.40     0.55</p>
<p> Income			     -1.68    -0.61     4.64</p>
<p> Transfers			  -5.22    -6.71     4.99</p>
<p>The ministry also gave the following seasonally adjusted data on the current account in billions of francs:</p>
<p>					 Nov	Oct     Sept</p>
<p> Current account		   7.98    13.38    17.16</p>
<p> Merchandise trade		 4.40     9.66     4.80</p>
<p> Services			    5.40     8.51     6.52</p>
<p>  -Travel			    4.36     6.42     4.58</p>
<p> Other goods and services	0.53     0.42     0.47</p>
<p> Income				0.91     3.66    -0.14</p>
<p>  -Investment income	     0.32     0.08     0.79</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
